  "details": "Good Day!\n\nUsing VCC v2.2.2 to create a Unity 2022.3 Avatar project creates a project without outdated packages (Timeline, TestMeshPro and TestFramework). Timeline can cause a script compile recursion when installing the Awtter SDK (ASDK).\n\nOur workaround is to upgrade to the latest available version within our scripts but we ask VRChat to update their project references to reflect Unity 2022 so we don't have to resolve to such nonsense.\n\nThis is our install script for additional packages. Without the line for \"com.unity.timeline\", the script compile process runs forever looping with Unity Timeline.\n\n```\n\nusing UnityEditor;\n\nusing UnityEditor.PackageManager;\n\nusing UnityEngine;\n\nnamespace AwtterSDK.Editor\n\n{\n\n    [InitializeOnLoad]\n\n    static class UPMImporter\n\n    {\n\n        static UPMImporter()\n\n        {\n\n            // VCC fix for Unity 2022.3.6f1\n\n            Install(\"com.unity.timeline\");\n\n            Install(\"com.unity.sharp-zip-lib@1.3.4-preview\");\n\n            Install(\"com.unity.nuget.newtonsoft-json\");\n\n            Install(\"com.unity.editorcoroutines\");\n\n            Install(\"com.unity.postprocessing\");\n\n        }\n\n        public static bool Install(string id)\n\n        {\n\n            var request = Client.Add(id);\n\n            while (!request.IsCompleted) { };\n\n            if (request.Error != null) Debug.LogError(request.Error.message);\n\n            return request.Error == null;\n\n        }\n\n    }\n\n}\n\n```\n\nThank you for your time.\n\nwith kind regards\n\nOomJan, Awtter Space Helper",
